    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **34 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule.\n\n**How the tier works:** `membershipTier` is a read-only field computed at DTO-mapping time (recomputed on every fetch), previously via a MapStruct expression in `OwnerMapper`. Since GOLD depends on the household's member count \u2014 not just the owner's own fields \u2014 the mapper needed access to the owner store.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 converted the MapStruct `interface` to an `abstract class` (MapStruct's component model is Spring, so the generated `OwnerMapperImpl` remains a bean) and:\n   - Injected `OwnerRepository` (`@Autowired protected`).\n   - Added `membershipTier(Owner)`: returns `GOLD` when the household (owners sharing the same non-blank `householdId`) has \u2265 3 members; otherwise falls back to the existing `SILVER` (namesakeCount == 0 and email present) and `BRONZE` rules.\n   - Added `isGoldHousehold(Owner)` which counts owners sharing the owner's `householdId` via `ownerRepository.findAll()`. An owner with no `householdId` is never GOLD.\n   - Pointed the `membershipTier` mapping expression at the new method.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` field description to document the GOLD rule (keeps API docs in sync with behavior).\n\nThe existing household-assignment logic in `OwnerRestControllerV1.assignHousehold` already converges housemates onto a shared `householdId` on each create, so by the time the third member is created all three share one id \u2014 yielding a count of 3 and GOLD. Existing SILVER/BRONZE tests (Cp15) and household tests (Cp11, Cp13) still pass, along with the new Cp23 test.",
